  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 103 AM EDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThe unsettled pattern will remain across South FL for the remainder \nof the upcoming work week. A broad upper level trough will remain \nover New England and the Mid Atlantic, with surface and upper level \nhigh pressure over the central Atlantic. The trough will likely \ndeepen across the eastern US as the week progresses as the high in \nthe Atlantic noses to the west. The area of enhanced moisture is \nexpected to remain across South FL for much of the week. With the \nlow/mid level flow remaining westerly, this will result in above \naverage PoPs across the east coast metro each day. While the \nrainfall will be much appreciated given the ongoing drought, will \nneed to be on guard for the potential of urban and poor drainage \nflooding each day across the metro. \n\nTemperatures during the extended period will remain above normal, \nwith high temps generally in the low to mid 90s and low temps \nranging from the middle 70s over inland South FL to around 80 closer \nto the coasts.",
